of what's to come for the rest of the weekend. :)"},{"business_id":"eca8IpdiY5ZNCgWAl4zXHQ","review_id":"Kbg7cYTQgvbAZ8jFvQnXeg","date":"2017-07-30T20:12:28","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.926041841506958,"text_excerpt":"We ate here twice. First was for drinks and beignets. Bartender very nice guy and knowledgeable. I had a nice Abita Blueberry Wheat, great summer drink. The beignets were pretty similar to cafe du monde, which we really like. Back the next day for lunch as we were inspired by the menu. It was good, chicken and waffles with a choice of standard maple or a pepper syrup, which was very good. Shrimp po boy was fair, fries were very good. Would recommend as a lunch spot. 3.5 probably closer to the mark"},{"business_id":"eca8IpdiY5ZNCgWAl4zXHQ","review_id":"ssid6Os6KAqj9aEXDvkR8A","date":"2017-01-21T16:38:28","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9173520803451538,"text_excerpt":"Went to new Legacy Kitchen in the CBD last night for a quick dinner. It's on Common and Baronne and has only been open 3 weeks. We were pleasantly surprised. The menu was heavy on oysters and each preparation that we tried was delicious. We cannot wait to go back and try other items on the menu. The mgr, Heather, was very attentive and made us feel like we were valued customers. Decent wine and beer selection. Welcome addition to neighborhood."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"eca8IpdiY5ZNCgWAl4zXHQ","photo_id":"9ssAZxJrvbTkJvNOfi_nHQ","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/9ssAZxJrvbTkJvNOfi_nHQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9256092309951782},{"business_id":"eca8IpdiY5ZNCgWAl4zXHQ","photo_id":"bEybk8dWyp8tBc9nTEnbFw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/bEybk8dWyp8tBc9nTEnbFw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8901008367538452},{"business_id":"eca8IpdiY5ZNCgWAl4zXHQ","photo_id":"fkiASL6YPxe_-DwWF_gt7w","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/fkiASL6YPxe_-DwWF_gt7w.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8561582565307617},{"business_id":"eca8IpdiY5ZNCgWAl4zXHQ","photo_id":"iywauD20WR